# Changes: comments removed; BFP_MAX_T raised from 32 to 256; `_ma_prepare` copies the gate/up rows in alygg77's KPERM3 order (`_kperm_rows`, as in alygg77/okc-muse-spark-kernels); `_bnd1_apply` and `_boundary1` read precomputed residual-gate alpha / beta instead of `_gate_ab`, and `_boundary1` also keeps the FP32 normalized activation for the router at T <= 8.
